# Copy to .env.local and fill in, or set the same name in your host's dashboard.
#
# Every value here is PUBLIC. NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at
# build time, so anyone who opens the site can read it. Never put a secret in this file
# or in any variable with that prefix — this app is a static export and has nowhere to
# keep one. See docs/ai.md.

# Google sign-in. Optional; leave empty and the app uses local profiles only.
#
# A browser OAuth client ID is public by design: it identifies the app and authorises
# nothing. What restricts it is the "Authorized JavaScript origins" list on the
# credential, which must contain the exact origin you serve from — for example
# http://localhost:3000 for development and https://your-app.vercel.app once deployed.
#
# Create one at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials (OAuth client ID,
# type "Web application"). Full setup notes in docs/google-sign-in.md.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is read at BUILD time, so setting this on a host requires a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
